{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And your name will be left as a curse.</b> ואלה is like ישימך כצדקיהו וכאחאב (Jeremiah 29:22), and a man will say to his fellow, 'May YHWH make you like…' (i.e., may one invoke your name as a curse)." "<b>He will call your name by another.</b> Honored."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {0 "Resolving the elliptical argument: Ibn Ezra quotes the Jeremiah formula where a name is used as a curse; the final phrase 'and a man will say to his fellow, May YHWH put you to death' appears garbled — likely a compressed or corrupt quotation of the curse formula."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:04.328739221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}